    { "id": "legend", "type": "rectangle", "x": 40, "y": 1975, "width": 1480, "height": 210, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#868e96", "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": [] },
    { "id": "legend-t", "type": "text", "x": 58, "y": 1986, "width": 1450, "height": 190, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": [], "text": "Key facts (from code):\n• Both kube-apiservers are ClusterIP Services — reachable from outside ONLY through an Istio IngressGateway LoadBalancer, routed by TLS SNI hostname.\n• Virtual garden and shoots use SEPARATE Istio ingress gateways (virtual-garden-istio-ingress vs istio-ingress) with DIFFERENT LB IPs.\n• gardener-apiserver: ClusterIP in runtime + a no-selector Service+Endpoints in the virtual cluster's kube-system pointing to the runtime ClusterIP; surfaced via APIService aggregation.\n• Reversed VPN (OpenVPN): vpn-shoot dials OUTBOUND via HTTP CONNECT to the seed IGW :8443 → vpn-seed-server. No inbound port on workers. The tunnel carries seed→shoot (pods/nodes/svc) traffic.\n• kubelet reaches the apiserver via apiserver-proxy → IGW :8443 (HTTP CONNECT), NOT over the VPN.\n• All virtual-garden-* and gardener-* control-plane pods physically run in the runtime cluster.\n• Kubeconfigs: [1] bootstrap → CSR, [2] gardenlet garden kubeconfig (X.509 CN=system:seed:<name>), [3] generic-token-kubeconfig (CA + token path), [4] shoot-access-* SA tokens, [5] static user (opt), [6] admin kubeconfig (on-demand, ephemeral).", "fontSize": 12, "fontFamily": 1, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null }
  ],
